      {
        "content": "## Summary\n\n**Target:** `F:ml430-int-gcd-div-5e01872f` — `Int.gcd_div`\n\n**Formal Statement:**\n```lean\n∀ {a b c : ℤ}, c ∣ a → c ∣ b → (a / c).gcd (b / c) = a.gcd b / c.natAbs\n```\n\n**Structural Shape:** This is a universally quantified equality involving integer GCD and division. It states that when `c` divides both `a` and `b`, the GCD of the quotients equals the quotient of the GCD by the absolute value of `c`.\n\n**Dependencies:** The fact has no dependencies and unlocks nothing. No registered operations target it.\n\n**Available Premises (Int prelude):**\n- GCD theorems: `Int.gcd_comm`, `Int.gcd_dvd_left/right`, `Int.dvd_gcd`, `Int.gcd_zero_right`, `Int.gcd_one_right`, `Int.gcd_eq_gcd_ab`\n- Division theorems: `Int.ediv_add_emod`, `Int.ediv_emod_unique`, `Nat.div_mul_cancel_of_dvd`, `Nat.div_mod_*` family\n- Also available: Nat-level GCD and division theorems\n\n**Similar Facts on Frontier:**\n- `F:ml430-int-gcd-div-gcd-div-gcd-2db608dc` (another Int GCD-division theorem)\n- `F:ml430-int-gcd-greatest-5b31c5fe` (Int GCD property)\n- `F:ml430-int-gcd-eq-gcd-ab-63005aef` (Bézout identity for Int)\n- `F:ml430-nat-div-dvd-div-left-b56f6f7c` (Nat division-divisibility)\n\nAll are in the Int fragment backlog with no registered operations.",
        "id": null,
        "provider_name": null,
        "provider_details": null,
        "part_kind": "text"
      }
    ],
