          "why": "The goal is a terminal equality involving GCD and division operations. The statement (a / c).gcd (b / c) = a.gcd b / c.natAbs requires proving an equality between two natural number expressions (since Int.gcd returns ℤ → ℤ → ℕ). This could potentially be closed by reflexivity if the kernel can normalize both sides to definitionally equal terms using the GCD and division computation rules.",
